  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes the typecheck. I couldn't run it in a browser, so I haven't seen a rendered frame, and the points below are unchecked.\n\n- **Bird:** it is built from spheres, boxes and a cone. There is a body, a head with a cone beak and two eyes, and a five-feather tail fan. Each wing has an inner and an outer box segment, hinged at the shoulder and at the inner tip.\n- **Flight:** the bird circles at radius 6 and height 4, one lap every 8 seconds. It faces along the path and banks inward by about 0.4 rad. Banking and heading use separate nested groups, so the result doesn't depend on the engine's rotation order.\n- **Flapping:** 2 flaps per second, so 16 flaps fit exactly in one lap and the loop has no jump. The outer segments lag the inner ones by about 0.8 rad. The body bobs by 0.1 units with each flap.\n- **Scene:** a ground disc with a few cone-and-cylinder trees, a sky-coloured background, a hemisphere light and one shadow-casting directional light.\n- **Camera:** it sits at radius 13.5, outside the circle, slightly behind the bird, and looks at it. I move it every frame with `app.camera?.setPose`. If `app.camera` is undefined in the browser, the camera stays at its starting pose and the bird will leave the view.\n- **Readiness:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()`.\n\nI left an unused `trees` variable in the file. It is harmless.",
